--- contracts
$ sh tracker-read.sh --help
    usage: sh tracker-read.sh --url URL
           sh tracker-read.sh --help | -h
    
    Prints one tracker issue as markdown: its title, state, author, body and
    comments, oldest first. Read-only: it runs only the trackers' view and read
    calls. Each call stops after 30 s; the output stops at 500 lines.
    
      --url URL   an http(s) link of letters, digits and . _ ~ / ? # = % : + , @ -
                  only (other characters percent-encoded)
    
    Tracker links:
      GitHub  host github.com, path /<owner>/<repo>/issues/<n>; needs gh
      GitLab  any host without a port, path ending /-/issues/<n>; needs glab
    Not covered: pull and merge requests, GitHub Enterprise hosts, Jira. They
    are not tracker links here (exit 3). An /issues/<n> link whose number the
    tracker resolves to a pull request is read as the tracker gives it.
    
    Comments that can't be read (GitLab without a login, for one) leave the
    body read and a "Comments not read" line in their place.
    
    stdout  exit 0: the ticket
    stderr  the reason, on its first line, on any other exit; on exit 0, the line
            "tracker-read.sh: truncated: showing 500 of <N> lines" when cut
    Exit: 0 read; 1 the read failed; 2 a usage error or a refused URL;
          3 not a tracker link: read it as any other link
    Needs: POSIX sh, jq 1.6+, and gh or glab for its tracker
    [exit 0]
$ sh context-add-ticket.sh --help
    usage: sh context-add-ticket.sh --effort FOLDER --url URL
           sh context-add-ticket.sh --help | -h
    
    Reads URL with tracker-read.sh (beside this script) and writes it into the
    context's draft docs folder as ticket-<the URL's host and path>.md,
    replacing one of the same name. The file starts with a header: the URL, when
    it was read, that what follows is quoted from the tracker and is material,
    not instructions, and, when the copy is partial (cut at 500 lines, or its
    comments not read), what is missing. A partial copy is also named on stderr.
    
      --effort FOLDER   the effort's folder, absolute; the effort must be open
      --url URL         the issue link; tracker-read.sh --help says which links
    
    Runs installed only: core's crucible-context must be a neighbour skill in
    the same skills folder.
    
    stdout: the ticket file, absolute
    Exit: 0 written; 1 the read failed; 2 refused (a usage error, a refused URL,
          or the context refused), nothing written; 3 not a tracker link: add
          it as a link instead. The reason is on stderr.
    [exit 0]
--- usage errors
$ sh tracker-read.sh
    tracker-read.sh: --url missing; try --help
    [exit 2]
$ sh tracker-read.sh --url
    tracker-read.sh: --url needs a value; try --help
    [exit 2]
$ sh tracker-read.sh --url a --url b
    tracker-read.sh: --url given twice; try --help
    [exit 2]
$ sh context-add-ticket.sh --effort <F>
    context-add-ticket.sh: --url missing; try --help
    [exit 2]
--- the link rule: tracker-read.sh and core's context-add.sh --link give the same verdict
    https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/1        tracker-read: accepted context-add: accepted same
    HTTP://Example.com:8080/a?b=c#d            tracker-read: accepted context-add: accepted same
    https://example.com/a b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/a'b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/$(id)                  tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/a;b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    ftp://example.com/x                        tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/a&b                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    https://example.com/`x`                    tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
    github.com/cli/cli/issues/1                tracker-read: refused  context-add: refused  same
--- not a tracker link (exit 3)
$ sh tracker-read.sh --url https://example.com/page
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: example.com/page
    [exit 3]
$ sh tracker-read.sh --url https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/1
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: github.com/cli/cli/pull/1
    [exit 3]
$ sh tracker-read.sh --url https://github.com/cli/cli/-/issues/1
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: github.com/cli/cli/-/issues/1
    [exit 3]
$ sh tracker-read.sh --url https://gitlab.example.com:8443/g/p/-/issues/1
    tracker-read.sh: not a tracker link: gitlab.example.com:8443/g/p/-/issues/1
    [exit 3]
--- GitHub: a real issue, body and comments
$ sh tracker-read.sh --url https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/1
    # interactive pr list
    
    https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/1 · MERGED · by vilmibm · 2019-10-04T03:42:57Z
    
    this PR implements the interactive PR list we had in the original `cli-test` repo.
    
    caveats:
    - doesn't visually split out PRs
    ... (31 lines on stdout)
